Widens the crash-forensics capture window for the ongoing freeze
investigation (docs/load-test-modules.md). The existing
ramoops@9fa00000 node (sm8250-samsung-common.dtsi, included by the
board .dts) already had a real 1MB pstore/ramoops carveout, just split
wastefully for this project's actual needs: 256KB each for
record/console/ftrace/pmsg. Neither CONFIG_PSTORE_FTRACE nor
/dev/pmsg0 userspace logging is in use, and the plain-text
console-ramoops backend is the only one that's actually produced
readable crash forensics all session (this device has a real
read-time bit-corruption problem, documented at length elsewhere in
this project - plain text survives it well enough to read around
individual garbled characters; a single bit flip anywhere in a
compressed dmesg-ramoops stream corrupts everything after it).

Every real hard-freeze capture before this change only had about one
second of runway before the crash (256KB filled fast at
printk/kmsg-injection sampling rates), not enough to see the lead-up
to a freeze rather than just its immediate aftermath.

Reallocates the same 1MB total: console-size 256KB -> 960KB
(0xf0000), ftrace-size and pmsg-size both dropped to 0. No new
reserved-memory region needed - stays within the existing carveout.

Status: built and tested. Confirmed a meaningfully longer capture
window (several seconds instead of under one) in subsequent crashes.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-samsung-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-samsung-common.dtsi
index ef7ea4f72..3be325069 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-samsung-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-samsung-common.dtsi
@@ -47,10 +47,25 @@ cont_splash_mem: memory@9c000000 {
 		ramoops@9fa00000 {
 			compatible = "ramoops";
 			reg = <0x0 0x9fa00000 0x0 0x100000>;
+			/*
+			 * Reallocated (2026-09-21, freeze investigation): the
+			 * ftrace-size and pmsg-size zones are dead weight here -
+			 * neither CONFIG_PSTORE_FTRACE nor /dev/pmsg0 userspace
+			 * logging is in use - while console-size (plain text,
+			 * survives this device's read-time bit corruption far
+			 * better than a compressed dmesg-ramoops record) is the
+			 * only backend that has actually produced usable crash
+			 * forensics all session. Every real capture from a hard
+			 * freeze so far only had ~1s of runway before the crash
+			 * (256KB filled fast at printk/kmsg-injection rates), not
+			 * enough to see the lead-up. Total stays within the
+			 * existing 0x100000 (1MB) carveout, no new reserved-memory
+			 * region needed. See docs/load-test-modules.md.
+			 */
 			record-size = <0x4000>;
-			console-size = <0x40000>;
-			ftrace-size = <0x40000>;
-			pmsg-size = <0x40000>;
+			console-size = <0xf0000>;
+			ftrace-size = <0x0>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x0>;
 			no-map;
 		};
 	};
